# WAVb: wavetables. Three parts, four beats each (a beat is 0.5 s):
#  0b..4b  a table of eight different noise cycles, swept from the first to
#          the last by `pos` (a glide): audible and in range;
#  4b..8b  the 440 Hz sine asset cut into 220 slices (two cycles each, so
#          the table is a clean sine), read at 220 Hz: a 440 Hz tone, within
#          5 cents, that glides up an octave in the last beat;
#  8b..12b the same table glided from 750 to 800 Hz (a 1.5 to 1.6 kHz tone) through three
#          steep high-passes at 13 kHz. Nothing of the table is up there
#          (its partials stop under 12 kHz at these pitches), so what is left
#          is what the reading made up: images and aliases. They are held
#          under -80 dBFS, 74 dB under the sine (-6 dBFS; measured -93.8 dBFS),
#          well past the -60 dB the plan asks of the top octave.
# scn: length 12b, seed 0, assets noise sine440
# expect: peak <= 0dbfs
# expect: rms 0.5b..3.5b >= -36dbfs
# expect: peak 0.5b..4b <= -15dbfs
# expect: pitch 4.5b..6.5b 440hz within 5c
# expect: rms 4.5b..6.5b >= -12dbfs
# expect: rms 8.5b..11.5b <= -80dbfs
# expect: equals golden
voice sweep gain=0.5 {
  wave t shape=table from="noise" slices=8 freq=220 pos=0
}
voice tone {
  wave t shape=table from="sine440" slices=220 freq=220
}
voice air {
  wave t shape=table from="sine440" slices=220 freq=750
  filter h1 type=hp cutoff=13000
  filter h2 type=hp cutoff=13000
  filter h3 type=hp cutoff=13000
}
start sweep
sweep.t pos=1 over 4b
wait 4b
stop sweep
start tone
wait 2b
tone.t freq=440 over 2b
wait 2b
stop tone
start air
air.t freq=800 over 4b
wait 4b
end after 12b
